/node_modules
# public/build IS tracked. The production host has no Node.js, so Vite cannot
# run there; the compiled assets have to arrive with `git pull` or the site
# renders unstyled. Run `npm run build` and commit the result whenever you
# change anything under resources/css or resources/js.
/public/fonts-manifest.dev.json
/public/hot
/public/storage
# Host artifacts, not project files. deploy/setup-website.sh creates the
# public_html symlink on the server (Hostinger will not change a Web plan's
# document root). Without this, deploy.sh's dirty-tree guard blocks every deploy
# because of a file the deployment itself created.
#
# /queue-worker.sh is gone from here and from the repo. The queue is now drained
# by `php artisan queue:drain` straight from the cron command, so there is no
# file in $HOME to be out of sync with the repository. A stale copy on the host
# is harmless but worth deleting.
/public_html
/public_html.hostinger-backup
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
_ide_helper.php
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db
/.claude
/DESIGN.md
